  Carry a reusable water bottle and coffee cup to avoid single-use plastics.
  Transition administrative workflows and sign-ups to paperless documentation.
  Set up home recycling systems for cardboard, plastics, and metals.
  Repurpose or upcycle organic waste unfit for human consumption by partnering with local farms or animal rescues.
  Divert food scraps from landfills by maintaining a backyard or community compost system.

2. Sustainable Food & Grocery Choices
  Plan weekly meals ahead of time to minimize discarded food waste.
  Bring reusable tote bags and mesh produce bags when shopping.
  Buy local produce and support regional agriculture to reduce food transit emissions.
  Host local drives or neighborhood exchanges to consolidate drop-offs and minimize total driving time.

3. Energy & Water Conservation
  Unplug electronics and appliances when not in use to eliminate standby energy draw.
  Switch household lighting to energy-efficient LED bulbs.
  Install low-flow showerheads and faucet aerators to decrease water usage.
  Lower thermostat settings in winter and raise them in summer by 2°F to save energy.
